# Keep secrets, local data, and bulky/irrelevant files out of ANY Docker build context.
#
# This is a safety net for both images — the app image (see Dockerfile) and the bridge
# image (see bridge/Dockerfile) — whose context is the repo root. Most importantly it
# guarantees a real `.env`, a webhook config, an exported snapshot/database, or a private key
# can never be copied into an image, even if one is present in the working tree.
#
# The bridge image copies `bridge/` wholesale into its *final* layer, so anything an operator
# keeps there travels wherever that image goes. The files they keep there are exactly the ones
# git refuses to track. The rule is therefore: **whatever `.gitignore` and `bridge/.gitignore`
# refuse to track, this file refuses to copy.** `src/lib/docker-context-ignore.test.ts` checks
# every rule in both of those files against this one, so the lists cannot drift apart.
#
# Sections below follow `.gitignore`'s own order, so the two read side by side.

# Logs
**/logs
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*
**/pnpm-debug.log*

# Dependencies / build output / caches — not needed in the build-free bridge image, and the app
# image builds its own `dist` (and fetches the OCR assets) inside the container.
**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store
**/dist
**/dist-ssr
**/*.local
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo
public/ocr/
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output

# Editor / OS / VCS / CI cruft.
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.suo
**/*.ntvs*
**/*.njsproj
**/*.sln
**/*.sw?
.git
.github

# Python tooling artefacts (the wiki/screenshot helpers).
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
**/*.egg-info
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# Secrets — never copy a real .env into an image (the placeholder .env.example is harmless
# but also unneeded at runtime, so it stays out too). `**/*.env` covers the un-dotted shapes
# `bridge/.gitignore` ignores, such as a `production.env` left beside the bridge.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env

# Bridge webhook targets — these hold per-target HMAC signing secrets and the `secrets` block
# that resolves `secret_ref` names, which is why `.gitignore` keeps them out of the repo. A
# signing secret in an image layer travels to every registry and host that image reaches. The
# committed `webhooks.example.json` is excluded too: it is documentation, not runtime config.
**/webhooks.json
**/webhooks.*.json

# The bridge's remembered identity — machine-local runtime state, not a secret, but baking one
# in would make every container built from the image claim to be the same bridge.
**/bridge-id

# Real inventory data must never enter an image (config points at a mounted snapshot).
**/local/
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.db
**/*.sql
**/gubbins-sync.json
**/gubbins-backup*.zip

# Keys, certificates, and keystores.
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.cer
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
**/id_rsa
**/id_rsa.*
**/id_dsa
**/id_ecdsa
**/id_ed25519

# Agent scratch space — `.claude/worktrees/` holds entire additional checkouts of this
# repository, which would otherwise be copied into the app image's build context.
.claude

# Local artefacts of the developer tooling.
scripts/.smoke-screenshot.png
.wiki/
